WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.018 --> 00:00:05.018
(dramatic music)
(rocket whooshing)

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.780
- We're here in southern Ukraine

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.930
where the military has
given us very rare access

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.930
to HIMARS, which are very
mobile artillery devices.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.090
The Americans have given the Ukrainians 16

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.983
of these since June.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:26.203
(soldier speaking in foreign language)

00:00:27.142 --> 00:00:28.650
(mechanism whirring)

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.150
- These HIMARS have been critical

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.940
to some of the recent
counteroffensives the Ukrainians

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.920
have launched against Russian positions.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.380
The systems carry usually six missiles,

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.650
which at the moment have
a range of 80 kilometers,

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.031
allowing the Ukrainians to strike deeper

00:00:43.031 --> 00:00:45.600
into Russian-held territory

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.973
than any other system they've had.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.260
The operators we spoke
to this week told us

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.620
that these HIMARS now make up 70%

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.050
of the firepower deployed
near the frontlines.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.660
These soldiers aren't allowed
by the Ukrainian military

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.091
to be identified by their names.

00:01:03.091 --> 00:01:07.674
(soldier speaking in foreign language)

00:01:17.895 --> 00:01:20.393
(rocket whooshing)

00:01:20.393 --> 00:01:22.680
- [Stephen] The HIMARS are
hitting everything at this point.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.280
Ammo depots, headquarters, bridges,

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.777
groupings of personnel, tanks, vehicles.

00:01:30.777 --> 00:01:35.360
(soldier speaking in foreign language)

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:47.430
(tank roaring)

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:49.530
- [Stephen] These weapon
systems have changed the course

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.210
of the war for Ukraine.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.510
They've allowed the military
to start pushing back,

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.210
taking back lands as they
have in the past few weeks,

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.467
both in the southern front,

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:01.433
as well as in Donbas and up in the north.

00:02:02.907 --> 00:02:07.490
(soldier speaking in foreign language)

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.500
- [Stephen] Russia's Defense Minister

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.670
has told Russian troops

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:24.210
to make Ukraine's long-range
weaponry a priority target

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.190
in a sign that Ukraine's
additional firepower

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.416
is taking a toll on Moscow's forces.

00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:30.420
(tank spinning)

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.760
Russia still occupies
large swathes of southern

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.900
and eastern Ukraine

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.780
and the US has promised
to send 18 more HIMARS

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.790
as part of a multi-year plan.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.530
But to fight off Russia's invasion,

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.050
Kyiv is also asking for
other advanced weapons,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.903
like tanks and fighter jets
from its Western allies.

